tests/queries/0_stateless/data_json/* binary
tests/queries/0_stateless/*.reference -crlf

# Long append-only lists of independent entries. Two pull requests that each add an entry almost
# always add it at the same place, and Git reports that as a conflict even though keeping both
# entries is always the right resolution. `merge=union` does exactly that, so these lists stop
# producing conflicts on GitHub.
#
# A union merge resolves every overlapping region by keeping both sides, which is only safe for
# a file that is nothing but such a list - hence the `.inc` files, which hold the list and no
# other code. Do not add `merge=union` for a file that has ordinary code in it.
#
# `src/Common/ErrorCodes.cpp` is deliberately absent: an error code is a value in the public
# protocol, and a union merge there would silently keep two entries with the same number.
src/Core/SettingsChangesHistory.cpp merge=union
src/Common/CurrentMetricsList.inc merge=union
src/Common/FailPointsList.inc merge=union
